WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.119
Now turn to Performance Review Blues at Riverside Community College.

2
00:00:04.319 --> 00:00:10.773
Dr. Sarah Chen supervises reference librarians Marcus Williams, Jennifer Park, and David Rodriguez.

3
00:00:10.973 --> 00:00:14.510
The narrative describes different reviews and subsequent tension.

4
00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.926
Read the full case before deciding what those events mean.

5
00:00:18.126 --> 00:00:22.507
Separate reported actions, characters' interpretations, and missing evidence.

6
00:00:22.707 --> 00:00:32.727
For your assigned AI conversation, ask for perspectives, explore alternatives, challenge possible consequences, and connect ideas to Chapters Ten through Twelve.

7
00:00:32.927 --> 00:00:38.831
Role-play can expose assumptions, but an imagined reaction is not evidence about a real character.

8
00:00:39.031 --> 00:00:43.637
Check whether the AI invents policies, budgets, motives, or citations.

9
00:00:43.837 --> 00:00:47.769
Ask which facts support its advice and what information might change it.

10
00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:53.316
Keep the complete, actual conversation, including your disagreements and changes of direction.

11
00:00:53.516 --> 00:00:55.880
Then write the required reflection yourself.

12
00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:01.607
Explain what the AI helped you notice, what it missed, and how you reached your own recommendation.

13
00:01:01.807 --> 00:01:06.654
Consult Canvas for submission details and the separate optional management simulation.

14
00:01:06.854 --> 00:01:10.743
This lesson offers preparation, not a completed case analysis.
